data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The developer claims the work is done. Per my brief: \"Check the developer's work yourself first. Run `cs-campaign-member fetch developer`, merge what comes back, build it, and look at the result.\" Then start the server once.\n\nOne thing to check: the README documents `npm run build` and `npm run serve`. The serve command — need to check what it is (probably `vite preview` or `npm run dev`?). The mission says serve on 0.0.0.0:5173 via the dev server. The developer said dev server bound to 0.0.0.0:5173 via vite.config.js. The serve command in README — let me look when I fetch.\n\nSteps:\n1. `cs-campaign-member fetch developer`\n2. Merge into my branch\n3. Inspect the code (App.jsx, package.json, README, vite.config)\n4. npm install, npm run build\n5. Start dev server once: `nohup npm run dev \u003e /tmp/dev-server.log 2\u003e\u00261 \u0026`\n6. curl the page, check it loads, check tokens, etc."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793343248,"id":"chatcmpl-51e4da75","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

